{title: 057 - Now All the Woods Are Sleeping}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Am]Now all [Dm/A]the woods are [Gm]sleeping,
[Am/E]And night and [C7]stillness creeping
[Gm]O'er city, [Dm/A]man, and beast;
[F/C]But thou, my heart, awake thee,
[C7/Bb]To pray'r awhile be take thee,
[Bb/F]And praise thy [C7]Maker ere [F/C]thou rest.

Verse 2:
[Am]My Jesus, [Dm/A]stay Thou [Gm]by me,
[Am/E]And let no [C7]foe come nigh [Dm]me,
[Gm]Safe sheltered [Dm/A]by Thy wing;
[F/C]But would the foe alarm me,
[C7/Bb]O let him never harm me,
[Bb/F]But still Thine [C7]angels round [F/C]me sing!

Verse 3:
[Am]My loved [Dm/A]ones, rest securely,
[Am/E]From every [C7]peril surely
[Gm]Our God will [Dm/A]guard your heads;
[F/C]And happy slumbers send you,
[C7/Bb]And bid His hosts attend you,
[Bb/F]And golden [C7]armed watch o'er [F/C]your beds.
